# mutgap_mem_reply_split: Info replies written across a page boundary where the next VA page's guest page is not adjacent (a leaf apart): the service's writable cursor over the reply buffer has two ranges there, and a sequential write that fills the first range goes on at the start of the second. 451 (heap texture size and align, 16 bytes) at reply offset 0x3ff8 puts 8 bytes at the end of VA page 8 and 8 at the start of VA page 9; a second 451 at 0x4010 lands wholly in page 9. Isolate only: in-process a reply aborts the host (info_reply_aborts_host). The values are the host's (s.metal gives them).
